      "ownershipVehicle": "ACP Crotona Holdings, L.P. / ACP Crotona Corp.",
      "description": "Corning Energy Corporation is the parent platform for regulated natural gas and electric distribution utilities in New York and Pennsylvania, including Corning Natural Gas Corporation, Pike County Light & Power Company and Leatherstocking Gas Company. Pike is an operating subsidiary rather than a separate manager-level infrastructure investment. Corning's operating history dates to 1904, its holding company was formed in 2013, and it acquired all of Pike's stock from Orange & Rockland on August 31, 2016. Argo Infrastructure Partners completed the acquisition of 100% of the Corning parent platform on July 6, 2022 through the ACP Crotona ownership chain. A 2025 application proposed replacing the Argo general partner with an Apollo-controlled general partner, but the transaction did not close and was terminated in January 2026. Argo therefore remains the current owner, and no signed pending ownership transaction was identified through August 16, 2026.",
